    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 8 · 4:18 · the butterfly rule</span>
      <strong>"Don't count how many butterflies there are"</strong>
      A framed picture of a tree covered in butterflies, and under it the level's most explicit instruction: <b>DON'T COUNT HOW MANY BUTTERFLIES THERE ARE! COUNT THE NUMBER OF BUTTERFLY PATTERNS THAT HAVE THE SAME COLOR</b>. Read it literally. The trick is that the butterflies are all different — you are counting how many share one colour scheme and wing pattern, not how many insects are on the tree. The easel on the left of the room holds the same butterfly tree, so the two are meant to be read together.
