      <strong>Turn the key, take the matches</strong>
      The desk drawer close-up shows a small silver <b>key</b> already sitting in the keyhole of the white top drawer, with the gold knob right beside it — you turn it rather than hunt for it. A few seconds later the <b>Matches</b> come into the inventory: a brown matchbox with the tray slid out and two neat rows of gold-headed matches, labelled simply <b>Matches</b>. Those matches are the tool for the box lid. Right after, the wardrobe opens at 5:24 — hanging clothes, folded stacks, and a dark green backpack on the middle shelf, with the wooden box from step 3 sitting on the top shelf.
