    </div>

    <div class="step-card">
      <span class="step-num">Step 10 · 6:00 · the switch chest</span>
      <strong>Four colours, sixteen switches</strong>
      A wooden chest with a brass latch opens as a close-up, and under the latch is the panel: <b>four coloured modules — red, yellow, green, purple — each holding four brass toggle switches</b>. Sixteen switches, all down when you find it. This is a state puzzle, not a code entry: the colours group the switches, and whatever pattern the room has been showing you is what you have to reproduce across the four groups.
